Package: shadowVIMP
Title: Covariate Selection Based on VIMP Permutation-Like Testing
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tim", "Mueller", , "mueller@staburo.de", role = "aut"),
    person("Oktawia", "Miluch", , "oktawia.miluch@staburo.de", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Staburo GmbH", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: A statistical method for reducing the number of covariates 
    in an analysis by evaluating Variable Importance Measures (VIMPs) 
    derived from the Random Forest algorithm. The method performs statistical 
    tests on VIMPs using permuted shadow variables to compute p-values, while
    preserving the correlation structure among predictors. It supports 
    multiple testing adjustments and outputs significance flags for each 
    covariate.
